@startuml phase1-handover
title Phase 1 — information handover\nENG to REG-LOCATION to MMS, over a live ISBM provider

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 12

actor "Engineer" as EngUser
actor "Location steward" as StewardUser
actor "Maintenance planner" as PlannerUser

box "SimHost — independent participants"
  participant "ENG" as Eng
  participant "REG-LOCATION" as Loc
  participant "MMS" as Mms
end box

participant "ws-ISBM provider" as Isbm

== Reference data ==

note over Eng, Mms
  Fixtures are deliberately asymmetric.
  ENG holds rdl:TemperatureIndicatingController.
  REG-LOCATION stops at rdl:Instrument.
  A library everyone held completely would make
  graceful degradation untestable.
end note

== Authoring — no messages ==

EngUser -> Eng : add tag TIC-106\nclass rdl:TemperatureIndicatingController\nrange 0..250 degC, action Reverse
activate Eng
Eng -> Eng : persist Tag
note right of Eng
  ENG's own vocabulary: TagNumber,
  ServiceDescription, PidReference.
  Nothing here is a Segment.
end note
Eng --> EngUser : WorkInProgress
deactivate Eng

== ENG's release event: named version promotion ==

EngUser -> Eng : promote "Rev F — Unit 101"
activate Eng
Eng -> Eng : validation gate

alt tag unclassified or incomplete
  Eng --> EngUser : 422 with findings — release blocked
else gate passes
  Eng -> Eng : Tag → Published\n+ Outbox row (one transaction)
  Eng --> EngUser : released
end
deactivate Eng

Eng -> Eng : build SyncSegments from committed rows
note right of Eng
  Spine carries identity and description.
  Class-governed values travel as
  properties with rdl: keys.
  ENG-local fields travel as eng: keys.
  The ancestor chain travels too, so a
  receiver can bind at a class it knows.
end note

Eng -> Isbm : POST sessions/{id}/publications\non /Enterprise/Site/Eng
activate Isbm
Isbm --> Eng : messageId
deactivate Isbm

== REG-LOCATION receives — arrival is not acceptance ==

Isbm -> Loc : GET sessions/{id}/publication
activate Loc

Loc -> Loc : bind class against the sender's chain

alt leaf class held
  Loc -> Loc : exact match
else leaf unknown, ancestor known
  Loc -> Loc : bind rdl:Instrument, flag degraded
  note right of Loc
    Partial understanding rather than
    all-or-nothing. The asset is still
    usable at a coarser class.
  end note
else nothing in the chain known
  Loc -> Loc : unbound — retained, not rejected
end

Loc -> Loc : ingest properties against the effective set
note right of Loc
  Two ranges map — rdl:Instrument confers them.
  rdl:ControlAction does not: its definition
  belongs to the leaf class REG-LOCATION lacks.
  Two eng: fields are unknown entirely.
  All three are retained and flagged.
end note

Loc -> Loc : queue StewardshipItem
deactivate Loc

StewardUser -> Loc : review queue
activate Loc
Loc --> StewardUser : proposal with binding state\nand mapped/unmapped counts

alt steward rejects
  StewardUser -> Loc : reject with reason
  Loc -> Loc : nothing enters the model,\nnothing republished
else steward approves
  StewardUser -> Loc : approve
  Loc -> Loc : Location LOC-000001\n+ Outbox row (one transaction)
  note right of Loc
    The registry does NOT adopt ENG's
    identifier. That is deliberate: a
    registry that reused the sender's key
    would have nothing to reconcile.
  end note
end
deactivate Loc

Loc -> Isbm : POST sessions/{id}/publications\non /Enterprise/Site/OandM
note right of Loc
  A new act by a different participant:
  new correlation id, new message id,
  rebuilt from REG-LOCATION's own rows.
  Not a forward.
end note

== MMS receives — and cannot tell what it has ==

Isbm -> Mms : GET sessions/{id}/publication
activate Mms
Mms -> Mms : assign legacy key 234441\nstore foreign id REG-LOCATION:LOC-000001\nCirid = null
note right of Mms
  MMS can only match a foreign identifier
  it has seen before. Another system
  describing the same pump under a
  different key is invisible to it.
end note
deactivate Mms

PlannerUser -> Mms : open equipment register
activate Mms
Mms --> PlannerUser : 234441 — resolved: false
deactivate Mms

note over EngUser, Isbm
  TIC-106, LOC-000001, 234441 — three systems, three identifiers,
  one physical pump, and nothing connecting them.

  This is the problem the ws-CIR resolves. Building it before the
  gap is visible would mean demonstrating a solution to something
  nobody had yet seen go wrong.
end note

@enduml
